#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Invoke (code name seance-chat): phone chat for Seance circles, with push notifications.

Runs next to the Seance daemon. A small web app (installable as a phone app) lists
circles; a message in a circle's thread becomes a Seance task for the circle's lead,
and the lead's `seance ctl finish` answer comes back as a reply and a phone
notification.

    seance-chat run           the server (a systemd user unit or a launchd agent)
    seance-chat alert TEXT    post TEXT to the Alerts thread and push it
    seance-chat digest        post the end-of-day summary to the Alerts thread
    seance-chat check         check the config and print what is missing, then exit

It listens on 127.0.0.1 only. Put something in front of it that adds a login header.
The simple way is `tailscale serve`, which gives it https and adds Tailscale-User-Login;
that login must equal OWNER. For a browser on the same machine with no Tailscale, set
LOCAL_MODE=1. Push needs cryptography and py_vapid (pip install -r requirements.txt).

Config: ~/.config/seance-kit/config.env (see config/config.env.sample). Any key can also
be set as an environment variable with the prefix SEANCE_KIT_. Keys made on first run
(vapid.pem, alert-token) live in the same folder. State (messages, read marks, push
subscriptions, open tasks) lives in ~/.local/share/seance-kit/.
"""

